# Project Rules — CodeJudgeX

## Identity

CodeJudgeX is a competitive programming judge for academic institutions.
Backend: Java 21 + Spring Boot 3 (modular monolith). Frontend: React 18 + Vite + TypeScript.
It is NOT a microservices system, NOT a Next.js project, NOT a Python project.

## Startup (mandatory before every response)

1. Read `.obsidian-ai-memory/02-PROJECTS/session-continuity.md`
2. Read `.obsidian-ai-memory/02-PROJECTS/project-context.md`
3. Read `.obsidian-ai-memory/03-ERRORS/error-memory.md`
4. Begin work — emit startup block

## Non-negotiable rules

- Memory read before any edit — no exceptions
- Never repeat a known error — check error-memory.md first
- No secrets in any file — ever
- Confirm before: rm, DROP TABLE, force push, hard reset, production migrations
- Verify before "done" — state test/typecheck result or explicitly state why not run
- Write session digest after every meaningful session
- Two-commit shutdown: code commit (feat/fix) + memory commit (memory: YYYY-MM-DD ...)

## Shutdown

Follow `.cursor/MEMORY-WORKFLOW.md` — all 10 steps. No abbreviations.
